course: dictionary
lesson: 8970
title: Single: one and only
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Single is a small word with a big job: it means only one, not two or more. «The first living things on Earth were tiny single cells in the sea.» Each living thing was one cell on its own, not many cells joined together.
explain: Look at the words around single to find its meaning. «Not a single» means none at all. «Not a single child in the class was late» means zero children were late, so the whole phrase tells you the meaning.
explain: The word after single can change what it suggests. A single room is for one person, and a single ticket is for going one way only. Try the swap check: put «only one» in place of single and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Single means only one, not two or more.
fact: «Not a single» means none at all.
fact: A single ticket (UK) is for going one way only, not there and back.
fact: A single is a song sold on its own. Singles is also a tennis game with one player on each side.
exercise: «A single short chirp every minute or so from a smoke alarm usually means its battery is low.» What does single mean here? | A loud alarm that never stops | Many chirps all at once | A chirp from a small bird | *One chirp, not a long run of them
exercise: «Not a single child in the class was late.» What does not a single mean? | All of the children together | Most of the children | *None at all | One child only
exercise: Mum says, «Get a single ticket, we are only going one way.» What kind of ticket is it? | A ticket for two people | A ticket for going one way only | A ticket for a bus with one seat | *A ticket for going one way only, not there and back
test: «The capital was put outside every state so that no single state would control the national government.» What does no single state mean? | Two states only | *Not one state, on its own, would have control | Only the biggest state | Every state, all together
test: A tennis game with one player on each side is called what? | matches | doubles | sets | *singles
exam: «They booked a single room in the hotel.» Which meaning of single fits best? | Not married | A song sold on its own | *Only one, made for one person | Going one way only, not there and back
